---
description: >-
  Three-lane query-escalation flow ("Head of Engineering", StatusSeeker,
  "Tech Lead") where an incoming query is routed up the chain until someone
  can answer it, using the dedicated `layout: swimlane` engine with both
  ignoreCrossLaneEdges and optimizeRanksByCrossings enabled. The "Head of
  Engineering" lane is declared first in the source, before the lanes that
  feed into it - unlike the sibling `8-query-process-2`, which declares
  lanes in flow order and omits the swimlane tuning options.
config:
  logLevel: 0
  flowchart:
    htmlLabels: false
    useMaxWidth: false
  layout: swimlane
  swimlane:
    ignoreCrossLaneEdges: true
    optimizeRanksByCrossings: true
---
swimlane-beta LR

  subgraph "Head of Engineering"
    E{Can answer?}
    E --Yes--> F(Answer)
    E --No --> G(Investigate) --> F2(Answer)
  end

  subgraph StatusSeeker
  A(Incoming query)
  A2{Knows<br/>which team?}
  end

  subgraph "Tech Lead"
    B{Can answer?}
    B --Yes--> C(Answer)

  end
  A --> A2
  A2 --Yes --> B
  A2 --No --> E
  B --No --> E
